N2  -  The risks associated with the isolated design of complex software systems within individual industries are analyzed, where not only the same thing is often done, but also the quality of the design suffers due to incomplete competence of the implementers. The approach of dividing competence and responsibility in complex software development by introducing an additional domain-specific layer of interaction between the software developer and the subject area specialists is discussed. The use of an adaptive modelling system as a tool for such separation is proposed. It is shown that the use of adaptive modelling as a common development platform for industry-specific CAD will not only improve the quality of production design in different industries, but will also simplify the design of production in related fields. Finally, it is shown that the use of a common platform will avoid the costs associated with the trend towards simplification and atomization of software developed in our country in the face of sanctions and the degradation of global connections. © 2022 New Technologies Publishing House. All rights reserved.

