N2  -  We introduce an entirely new class of high-order methods for computational fluid dynamics based on the Gaussian process (GP) family of stochastic functions. Our approach is to use kernel-based GP prediction methods to interpolate/reconstruct high-order approximations for solving hyperbolic PDEs. We present a new high-order formulation to solve (magneto)hydrodynamic equations using the GP approach that furnishes an alternative to conventional polynomial-based approaches. © 2017, The Author(s).

