N2  -  In cementing operations, real-Time control of slurry density and equalizing tank liquid level is crucial for cementing quality. Traditional control methods struggle to effectively resolve the coupling problem between these two parameters and exhibit insufficient disturbance rejection capabilities. To address these challenges, this paper proposes a feedforward-compensated zone model predictive control method (FC-ZMPC). This approach employs setpoint control for slurry density and zone control for the equalizing tank liquid level to prevent the impact of frequent level fluctuations on density. Meanwhile, it incorporates the pump injection rate as a measurable disturbance into the model prediction process for dynamic feedforward compensation, enhancing the system's disturbance rejection capability. Simulation results demonstrate that compared to PID control and active disturbance rejection control methods, FC-ZMPC exhibits superior control performance under various conditions, significantly reducing adjustment time, overshoot, and steady-state error. It effectively improves the stability and accuracy of slurry density control while maintaining the liquid level within a safe operating range. This method provides a new, effective approach for automated and intelligent control of the cementing slurry mixing process. © 2025 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).

