N2  -  In modern machining operations use of process data drives future machining standards. Machining process data reach from the geometrical data over validated process parameters (e.g. speeds, feeds, depth of cut) up to simulation data to describe physical process impact on components surface integrity. The effective data use in production depends on verification of its physical relevance and knowledge of process control limits. In this paper examples of different types of machining process modelling and data usage are set into context of turbine disc machining. This concludes in a definition of an appropriate level of process modelling on today's applications. © 2019 The Authors. Published by Elsevier B.V. Peer-review under responsibility of the scientific committee of The 17th CIRP Conference on Modelling of Machining Operations

