N2  -  This paper continues the previous research on transforming BPMN models into Colored Petri Nets (CPNs). The prior study introduced the PetriBPMN methodology, which automated the conversion of BPMN-Light models into Colored Petri Nets, facilitating process simulations. Building on this foundation, the current research presents a new subclass of CPN, termed CPN-Light, aimed at enhancing simulation capabilities while maintaining modeling simplicity. CPN-Light models introduce a developer-friendly syntax inspired by C#, simplifying formal modeling without compromising CPN capabilities. Additionally, the paper introduces the ongoing development of a new tool intended as a modern alternative to CPN Tools, which is now out of support, ensuring continued accessibility and usability for process modeling and simulation. The new simulation tool will complement this by enabling simulation, visualization, and debugging of transformed models. Furthermore, BPMN-light models can be annotated and observed directly through synchronized CPN-Light visualizations, significantly enhancing process transparency and simulation feedback.  © 2025 The Authors. Published by Elsevier B.V.

