N2  -  To address the existing challenges from lack of virtual reality teaching cases, insufficient interactivity, limited display, and insufficient integration of digitalization and three-dimensional visualization in the existing majors of automatic control and environmental engineering, this study considers the automatic control scenario of precise aeration process in the new rural sewage treatment system, then to enrich the teaching cases of virtual reality. A process model for precise aeration of sewage based on a fuzzy controller was established, and a simulation model for automatic control of the process was constructed in Simulink of MATLAB. The dissolved oxygen content of the biological tank is measured with the sensors in the sewage aeration process, and the dissolved oxygen requirement of the biological tank in the sewage treatment system is calculated. The national standard value for controlling the dissolved oxygen content is set as the control target. The high-pressure fan precise aeration principle is adopted to compensate and control the dissolved oxygen content of the biological tank. This study designs a fuzzy PID controller for precise aeration and uses virtual reality (VR) technology to dynamically display the curves and trends of the measured dissolved oxygen content in the biological tank and the control target value. By interactively adjusting the proportional, integral, and derivative parameters of the PID controller online, multiple sets of control performance curves are formed to achieve interactive digital teaching effects. This study will enrich the digital teaching cases for both automatic control major and environmental engineering major in the field of new rural sewage treatment, and can also provide technical references for empowering smart water treatment with artificial intelligence and promoting the cultivation of compound and scarce talents in this field.  © 2025 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).

